IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ro-orders`
IMPORT `ro-qa`

-- Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (ro-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation ("it is an assumed
-- term"). Each question that takes the situation input is asked, for its own role, with each value of `the order so
-- far` under which it does not arise, every later input ASSUMEd: again `does not arise for you`. For the protected
-- person (the baseline's seat) answers are also asserted equal to the baseline export's own answer on the same facts.
-- For the respondent the answers are worked by hand from the text; mirror cases ask one order from both seats.
--
-- Not every "not read" claim rests on a case. `the order so far` is read only through helpers that list every value
-- with no OTHERWISE, so an ASSUMEd value read there fails. But the baseline reads `Kind of order` through CONSIDER ...
-- OTHERWISE (its breach and duration rules), and its records only through field access, so for an ASSUMEd kind,
-- relationship or case the order of the checks is shown by the parameter script and the code as well as by the cases
-- (graffiti D8.8).
--
-- Facts: Jake, k063 (22 August 2036), and the baseline's fixtures and variants, copied from ro-cases-orders.l4 (a case
-- file cannot be imported without running its assertions). Expected values are written by hand from the deposited
-- text, never copied from the output.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked order so far` IS A `The order so far`
ASSUME `an unasked kind` IS A `Kind of order`
ASSUME `an unasked relationship` IS A `The relationship between us`
ASSUME `an unasked deed` IS A `What the respondent has done to me`
ASSUME `an unasked case` IS A `My case`
ASSUME `an unasked applicant` IS AN `Applicant`

`as the protected person` MEANS `I want to be protected from someone`
`as the respondent` MEANS `someone wants a restraining order against me, or one has been made against me`

`no order yet` MEANS `no order has been made yet`
`interim order made` MEANS `an interim order has been made`
`final order made` MEANS `a final order has been made`
`police order made` MEANS `a police order has been made`

§§ `Fixtures (the baseline's)`


